==== Assumption #1: does multi-sieving dissolve the apex obstruction? ====
  configs containing a multiple of 14 (apex-stuck at m=14): 2366
   caught by m=14 alone:           0/2366 (0.0%)
   caught by some m in {2..13}:    2154/2366 (91.0%)
   => apex-stuck-at-14 configs rescued by a DIFFERENT modulus:
        (4, 6, 11, 14, 17, 20, 24, 39, 43, 48, 55, 56, 59)  caught at m=9
        (2, 3, 11, 18, 21, 24, 25, 28, 30, 33, 34, 42, 56)  caught at m=13
        (2, 9, 12, 15, 16, 21, 24, 33, 42, 50, 51, 55, 59)  caught at m=13
   The apex is a single-modulus artifact; multi-sieve has no apex.

multi-sieve residual shrinkage over 329 configs (random + loaded):
  div{2..14} alone:        caught 292/329 (88.8%)
  fold (recursive) alone:   caught 283/329 (86.0%)
  div{2..14} OR fold:      caught 313/329 (95.1%)
  div{2..28}:              caught 329/329 (100.0%)
  PINCH (pair-sum moduli):  caught 329/329 (100.0%)  <- COMPLETE
  largest min-division-modulus among the div+fold residual: 23  (S551 unboundedness)
